  "responseText": "{\"reviewedAffectedSlots\":[\"W010\",\"W123\"],\"findings\":[\"W010 (nnxyz nifty faces #40): The corrected white-canvas image reveals a white ground, not the dark or neutral ground implied by the earlier description. The face is densely packed with multicolored short strokes — magenta, cyan, red, yellow, orange — visible throughout the entire composition including the margins. The eye sockets contain rounded squares with cross marks, and the surrounding field is a riot of overlapping colored dashes and scribbles extending to the canvas edge, with no dark suppression of those marks. The mouth zone shows wide rounded tooth shapes in white with colored underlayers visible. The description of 'white ground' was correct in the existing prose, but the characterization of 'short color strokes' understated the chromatic intensity: the corrected image shows the full spectrum of dense multicolored marks radiating across the whole canvas, not merely packed between black scaffolding. The black scaffolding is present but the colored strokes are equally dominant and highly saturated, not subordinate to the black structure.\",\"W123 (nnxyz nifty faces #14): The corrected white-canvas image shows a saturated yellow ground filling the entire canvas. The face interior is densely packed with multicolored scribbles — magenta, purple, teal, green, red — far more chromatic and visually complex than 'steep diagonal black lines over the eyes' suggests. The eye rectangles contain layered colored marks with small dark spiral centers, not simply diagonal hatching. The mouth bar is a white horizontal rectangle with sparse black tick marks, clearly sealed and pale against the surrounding color density. The overall field is extremely busy with looping white lines in the yellow margins and dense colored scribbles filling the face mass. The prior description emphasized black diagonal lines as the dominant feature, but the corrected image shows the face interior is primarily a dense multicolored scribble field, with the yellow ground and white mouth bar as the clearest structural anchors. The transition description referencing 'steep diagonal hatching' and 'no opening' also needs revision to reflect the actual chromatic density visible.\"],\"membershipConcerns\":[],\"corrections\":[{\"slot\":\"W010\",\"whyHere\":\"Cross marks inside rounded-square eye sockets anchor the compartment logic, but the corrected image reveals the entire canvas — face and margins alike — filled with dense, equally weighted multicolored strokes in magenta, cyan, red, yellow and orange, all reading at full saturation against the white ground. The black scaffolding organizes the zones without suppressing the chromatic field around it, making this the most chromatically pressurized face in the chapter.\",\"transitionFromPrevious\":\"nnxyz nifty faces #101's density was built from crossing lines alone; nnxyz nifty faces #40 replaces that linear accumulation with a full-spectrum field of short colored strokes — magenta, cyan, red, yellow, orange — packed across every zone and into the margins, so the interior pressure is chromatic rather than purely linear.\"},{\"slot\":\"W123\",\"whyHere\":\"A saturated yellow ground fills the canvas edge to edge, and the face interior is a dense mass of multicolored scribbles — magenta, purple, teal, green, red — with looping white lines circling through the yellow margins. The eye rectangles hold layered colored marks converging on small dark spiral centers, and the mouth is a sealed white horizontal bar with sparse black tick marks: the one clear pause in an otherwise unrelenting chromatic density.\",\"transitionFromPrevious\":\"nnxyz nifty faces #106's loose lines spread across a yellow-green field; nnxyz nifty faces #14 replaces that open scatter with a compressed mass of multicolored scribbles packed tightly into the face volume, the yellow ground pressing in from every edge while the white mouth bar holds as the sole uncluttered zone.\"}],\"chapterCorrections\":[]}",
